Z||000001||Formula 18||10-14-2000||09:37 AM||||You might be better off too look for a little larger turbo. A garrett T-3 from a Thunderbird if your searching the bones yards or a T3/4 Hybrid if you have lots of money. <P>here's a site that details putting a kit in for under a grad. <P> <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-15-2000||01:33 AM||||So The 2.0 turbo WON'T WORK on the 2.8L ??<BR>What kind of HP difference would it be adding the 2.0L turbo to the 2.8L ???<BR>              thank's Steve||||reg||6
Z||000003||Formula 18||10-15-2000||09:25 PM||||It might work, it might spool up so quick it would only be a exuast blockage too. I would look for a T3 instead of the T25. It has a slightly larger housing for the increased displacment. <P>Brian  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||10-16-2000||02:58 PM||||I can get a fresh turbo off a chrysler laser 2.2 liter I4, but I would blow my motor up...  <BR>would that turbo work?||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||10-16-2000||03:36 PM||||a T25 / T28 and T28(super 60) would have to be run in pairs to support the 2.8. a pair of T3s would get you the same basic performance that the design one kit has with less heat cause they would have to work less to hold 10psi and would transfer less heat giving you a little better performance. a T-04e is what you'd need for a nice single turbo setup. it'ss ramp up @ 1500-2200 and not run hot or hard on the highway. where the smaller ones will GLOW on a longer trip. a TD-06 16g from a Typhoon or Cyclone would be the best.. ok for daily driving no real boost till 25-3000rpm then it'll SMASH you in the back of the head like a sledghammer! <A HREF="http://www.turboneticsinc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turboneticsinc.com</A>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  i've got some.. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||10-16-2000||04:18 PM||||    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/airneed_copy.jpg">    <P>the air flow needed to support a given displacement at a given boost level. as you can see we need 20+lbs/ per minute of air... <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/t3.jpg">    <BR>the base T3 is STRUGGELING to make that thus you need two! while the ...<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/t6.jpg">    <P>T6 makes 20lbs/min with no flinch.. but the engine will be at a higher RPM... making less heat, using less fuel.  just a few things i learned in College...     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Ga. Techs COOL!<P><BR>thanks to Turbonetics too... <A HREF="http://www.turboneticsinc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turboneticsinc.com</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg">    <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
