Z||000008||gamman||10-17-2000||02:23 AM||||good idea for a twin turbo idea, but good luck sorting. I personally would pay a premium for a good set up tubes so I can bolt on some 2.0 turbos onto a 2.8 or bored 3.1.  But, getting it to this level for resale, an engineer I am not.  <P>I do know how to test a turbo, and get one from a scrapyard, and bolt on a set of exhaust pipes and intakes. Does that make me a hero??<P>Has anyone ever done this or seen someone who has??<P>Gerry.||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||10-17-2000||08:15 AM||||there are a couple guys on here with Turbo set-ups.. I have 2 T-28(super 60)s and one TD-06 super 16g... i'm rounding up a liquid to air intercooler and the line to run to the front for the heat exchanger... i'll let you know how it turns out... these guys are doing the actual fabrication...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  <A HREF="http://cnmmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://cnmmotorsports.com/</A> <P>same guys that tuned my 86 SE to run 14.7 all motor! with no major mods.<P>2 T-25s would be GREAT! they'd spool up quick and EASILY support 10psi... so go find 2 wrecked 90-98 Eclipse turbos! and your set.<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-17-2000||10:47 PM||||1fast.... What is the diierence between the turbo from the Sunbird vs. the Eclipse 's turbo????  could I mix and match by using one from each, If that's the only way I can find them...????   <BR>                           Thank's for info.<BR>                              Steve||||reg||1
Z||000011||Yellow85||10-18-2000||05:44 AM||||You can't find T-too small (T-25) in the 90-94 eclipse.  90-94 eclipse got TDO5H-14B, it flow 405 CFM@15psi.  These turbo spool up quick and as far as I know, they won’t have heat problem if you run at less than 1 bar (with intercooler).  TDO6-16G(550 cfm)  is really big turbo compare to T-25 or 14B.  Don’t  know how fast they will spool up with fiero engine though.  Most of 16Gs will spool up to full boost at somewhere around 3000-3500rpm(on most of the engine).  If you want to have a turbo that spool up faster, find ball bearing turbo, they will spool up faster.  By the way, any big turbo won’t work good without free exhaust, intercooler, more fuel and also lowered compression engine(to run higher boost).<P>P.S. <BR>This is just my opinion, so it may not be all true since I don’t know how well Fiero engine work with turbo(I never had turbo charged fiero).<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000012||1FST2M6||10-18-2000||08:16 AM||||Yellow is right... lower compression will help reduce detonation. but with out a rebuild just add water... water injection will drop the combustion temps and stop nasty detonation. the Sunbird and eclipse turbos are different they have different exhaust wheels. the compressor wheels are the same (according to turbonetics) so 2 eclipse or 2 sunbird turbos... 2 turbo coupe.. etc.. as long as they match you'll be ok.. the 90-94 Capri XR2 turbos are nice.. internal waste gates with adjustable pressure valves (vacuum and mechanical) the nice-cute-tiny intercooler will fit where your factory intake canister is... (i'll get a pic this weekend) you can usually find these in decent shap in bone yards.. or an XR4Ti will work ok. but you'll have to message the deck lid a little. proper ignition timing and boost sensative fuel pressure is needed too... vortec SFMU, and MSD 6BTM. along with RC injectors. <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rceng.com</A>  you can run 10psi with out any real problems with the botom end... and more with and intercooler and even MORE with water injection!  <A HREF="http://www.f-max.com" TARGET=_blank>www.f-max.com</A>  for water injection<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||1
